=== REASONING ===

Problem: When a charge session ends, enhancedFields are built from accumulated session
data (temp sums, location). If Tesla delta encoding means temp or location signals weren't
sent during the charge (e.g., car was already parked and temps stable), those fields are nil.

Solution: Use SnapshotAt() from signal_history as a fallback to reconstruct signal state
at charge end time. Insert enrichment block between enhancedFields construction and the
WithTx transaction boundary.

Fields enriched:
- latitude, longitude ← endSnapshot["Latitude"], endSnapshot["Longitude"]
  Also sets active.Latitude/active.Longitude so downstream geocoding triggers
- inside_temp_avg_c ← endSnapshot["InsideTemp"] (when insideAvg is nil)
- outside_temp_avg_c ← endSnapshot["OutsideTemp"] (when outsideAvg is nil)

Constraints satisfied:
- Existing enhancedFields construction preserved (primary path)
- signal_history is fallback only (_, ok check before each field)
- SnapshotAt errors are non-fatal (log.Warn and continue)
- signal_history reads happen BEFORE the transaction boundary
- Uses signalHistoryWriter already wired by prompt 04
- startSnapshot fetched but unused for field enrichment (charge is stationary)
  — assigned to _ to avoid unused variable error

